task_id: sql_0030
task_type: sql
instruction: "The SQLite database 'Database for tasks.sqlite3' in the current directory has tables: CATEGORY(WARE, CLASS) - which category (CLASS) a ware belongs to (a ware may belong to several categories); MANUFACTURER(BILL_ID, COMPANY) - bills of materials and the companies owning them; MATERIAL(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT) - materials used by a bill; PRODUCT(BILL_ID, WARE, AMOUNT, PRICE) - wares produced by a bill, with amount and price. A bill may produce several wares. Show one sample ware from each category (the alphabetically first ware of the category). Write one row per line as category;ware, sorted by category name. Compute the answer with bash (sqlite3 and/or python3). Work only inside the current directory. When you are done, write ONLY the final answer to the file answer.txt in the current directory (for example with bash: echo 42 > answer.txt)."
reward: 3
expected: "Chemicals;Charcoal\nFood;Drinking water\nFuel;Charcoal\nLivestock;Meat cow\nMineral;Gold ore\nRaw food;Grain\nRaw material;Wood\nReady food;Drinking water\nStuff;Gold"
check: exact_str